{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1551896595,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTc5NDUzNzE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3204","origin":"github"},"title":"add's --to-annex is unreachable","message":"I was looking at command-line options that use `dest=` to see if there are any other options that flip like `--nosave -\u003e save` and thus have the same problem described in #3203.  I didn't spot any, but I did get confused by `add`s `--to-annex`:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/c3fe0350b12c2001b24d400a0b3c2b4a5f156013/datalad/distribution/add.py#L150-L159\n\nIt reuses `--to-git`s variable by design: 49f296ba7 (ENH: add --to-annex (reuse to_git Python interface though) to force adding to annex, 2017-07-26).  There is a [comment] in the corresponding PR that said \"seems to work\", but it doesn't work now (c3fe0350b):\n\n```\n% datalad add --to-annex blah\n[ERROR  ] unknown argument: --to-annex\nusage: datalad add [-h] [-d PATH] [--to-git] [--nosave] [-m MESSAGE]\n                   [-F MESSAGE_FILE] [-r] [--recursion-limit LEVELS] [-S]\n                   [--git-opts STRING] [--annex-opts STRING]\n                   [--annex-add-opts STRING] [-J NJOBS]\n                   PATH [PATH ...]\n```\n\n[comment]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/1652#issuecomment-318089627","files":null}]}